cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ScienceBro: an independent verification workbench for machine-learned spacetimes"
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andrey
    family-names: Pluzhnik
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # fill in after registering
abstract: >-
  A research workbench for auditing machine-learning claims in general relativity. It
  contains an independent finite-difference curvature evaluator (Ricci, Kretschmann,
  Weyl/Petrov speciality index, trapped-surface diagnostics) that shares no code with the
  systems it audits, a deterministic proof-gate system in which stage statuses are computed
  from hashed artifacts rather than asserted, and the first independent audit performed with
  it: the AInstein black-hole search (arXiv:2607.05489).
keywords:
  - general relativity
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - independent verification
  - reproducibility
  - Petrov classification
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PLACEHOLDER/sciencebro"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Black Hole Black Boxes: Machine learning solutions to the Einstein field equations"
    authors:
      - family-names: Hirst
        given-names: Edward
      - family-names: Schettini Gherardini
        given-names: Tancredi
      - family-names: Stapleton
        given-names: Alexander G.
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2607.05489"
    notes: "The work audited by this software. Its upstream code is GPL-2.0 and is kept isolated."
